# System Processes Guide

This guide describes the core system processes available in the 00OS environment.

## Core System Commands

The system processes provide fundamental functionality for the 00OS environment:

### Help Command
The [help.md](mdc:00OS/processes/system/help.md) command is the primary way to get information about available commands:
- Use `help` without arguments to list all available commands
- Use `help <command>` to get detailed help for a specific command
- Supports both system and reaper commands

### Version Command
The [version.md](mdc:00OS/processes/system/version.md) command displays system version information:
- Use `version` for basic version info
- Use `version --detailed` for comprehensive system information
- Shows information about core components and build status

## Usage in Development

When developing new features or modifying existing ones:
1. Always check command documentation using the help system
2. Use version information to ensure compatibility
3. Follow the established command patterns for consistency:
   - Support `--help` flag for all commands
   - Use standardized status indicators (✅/❌)
   - Implement comprehensive error handling

